  "notes": "Cash-basis village, one fund-type split. Governmental receipts from Total Governmental Funds column (p4); disbursements by function from the Statement of Activities p2 (p4 shows only by object: personnel 198,638, operating 187,110, supplies 54,351, payroll taxes 83,599, capital 146,028; same 669,726 total). Business-type from proprietary statement p6 total column (Water, Sewer, Electric); loan proceeds 634,321 recorded in business_type.debt_proceeds, not receipts. Business-type receipts total is not printed as one number; computed as operating revenues plus interest income. Fund-level transfers 541 in/out net to zero in the total column. Detail: p7 all-funds budget schedule is combined; mixed lines (sales taxes, interest, charges, other) split by fund type using p2/p4/p6 and p2 program revenues; budget_final left null on split lines. SRF 634,321 printed inside Total receipts so recorded as other financing with includes. p8 County Treasurer's Fund schedule is not recorded in detail: it is a pass-through whose receipts (83,084 less collection fee 579 = 82,505) are the same money as the p4 'County treasurer receipts' line and the p7 county treasurer receipts/tax credit/pro rate/carline lines (no double counting). Its breakdown: property taxes 57,846, motor vehicle taxes 12,574, motor vehicle prorate 133, personal property tax credit 7,869, homestead 4,438, carline 177, interest 47; transfer to Village Treasurer 81,496. Trimmed PDF has 8 pages; p1 report p8, p2 p9, p3 p10, p4 p11, p5 p12, p6 p13, p7 p27, p8 p28. Read pages 1-8 of 8 Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p4, p6) replace the combined schedule."
